What is dataflow in ADF
	A data flow in Azure Data Factory is a visual, code-free transformation feature that lets you design data transformation 
  logic (such as filter, join, aggregate and derive columns) on a graphical canvas. ADF converts the design into Spark code and executes it on a 
  managed Spark cluster, reading from source datasets and writing the transformed result to sink datasets.
	    A data flow in ADF is a GUI-based way to build data transformations at scale. You define a source, apply transformations, 
      and write to a sink, and ADF runs it on a managed Spark cluster without you writing any code


Types of DataFlows in ADF

Type                  |						Purpose				                                                      |			Engine
----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------
Mapping Data Flow     |	Visual, code-free transformations (source → transformations → sink) at scale  |	Managed Spark cluster
Wrangling Data Flow   |	Power Query-style data preparation with a spreadsheet-like UI		              |	Power Query Online, translated to Spark



